# Glossary

Terms used by the documents and rules of this repository. The meta-repository terms come with the template; project terms are added below them as they appear, one row each.

## Meta-repository

| Term | Meaning |
| --- | --- |
| Meta-repository | This repository. It holds the shared agent rules, OpenSpec, decisions and checks, and contains the clones of the application repositories. It has no application code. |
| Clone | A folder in `repos/` with its own `.git`, for example `repos/api`. The meta-repository does not track it. |
| Registry | The file `repos.toml`, the only list of repositories with their URLs, rest branches, branch models and stacks. Other lists are generated from it with `mise run repos:sync`. |
| Rest branch | The branch a clone stays on between tasks, its `ref` in `repos.toml`, usually `dev`; it is deployed to the test server. |
| Branch model | How a clone's work branches start and end: `main-based` (from `main`, into `dev` for QA, then into `main`) or `dev-based` (from `dev`, into `dev`; `main` receives only merges of `dev`). |
| Merge branch | A branch `merge/<name>-into-dev` of a main-based clone, created from `dev` when a work branch conflicts with `dev`. It receives only merges of its work branch and carries the pull request into `dev`. |
| Clone backlog | The file `docs/clone-backlog.md` with changes that would be useful inside the clones but were deliberately not made from the meta-repository, each with a reason. |
| Kit clone list | The file `openspec/clones`, through which sdd-kit knows the clones. It is generated from the registry. |
| Change | An OpenSpec change in `openspec/changes/`: questions, proposal, specs, design, tasks. Kept only in the root. |
| Spec | The requirements of one capability in `openspec/specs/`, with scenarios. |
| Single check | The `mise run check` command. It runs every clone's own linters and type checks and the root's shared checks. |
| Rule | An `ast-grep` check in `ast-grep/rules/` with a test in `ast-grep/rule-tests/`. |
| ADR | A decision record in `docs/adr/`, with a number and a status. |
| `main` | In a clone, the production branch; in the meta-repository, the only long-lived branch. The agent never commits or pushes to it. |

